<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      A month in the calendar is marked by a BOUNDARY, not by filling a block of days (DESIGN §5, PRD 5.3).
      We add cal-month-line and remove cal-othermonth and cal-othermonth-weekend: they
      no longer have a reader.

      Why the fill was removed. It answered the question "own month or other", i.e. it
      depended on where the window stood. With week paging the window started moving, and
      the anchor crossed a month boundary every 4-5 clicks: at that moment up to 28 cells
      out of 28 changed tone AT ONCE, from a one-week step. A one-week movement did not read;
      it read as flipping pages (noticed by the owner on the live board: "no feeling
      that this is one canvas going back").

      Why the boundary does not have this problem: it belongs to the SEAM between two days and moves together with
      it. A single day's look stopped depending on the window position at all: that is exactly
      "one canvas".

      The same edit removed the dimming of the other month's figure (text-secondary): it was the same
      signal and would invert in exactly the same way, just quieter. The separate token for
      the other month's weekend (0310) loses its meaning with it: there is now exactly
      one weekend in all months of the window.

      The line's shade: we take the tile border (wave 01's border-tile): the calendar and the widget's edge
      speak one line language, and it is not a new colour on the board but an already accepted one. Wave 02
      draws its own edge (cloud cards), so it gets the graphite of its own ink.

      NB: surface-othermonth is NOT touched: it paints the "Today" tile when a day of another
      month is selected (§4), is counted from today and does not change on paging (paging does not change
      the selected day).
    -->
    <changeSet id="0340-wave-01-month-line" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET tokens = (tokens - 'cal-othermonth' - 'cal-othermonth-weekend')
             || $J${"cal-month-line": "#d58b69"}$J$::jsonb
WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET tokens = (tokens - 'cal-month-line')
             || $J${"cal-othermonth": "#ece0d7", "cal-othermonth-weekend": "#e3d2c5"}$J$::jsonb
WHERE key = 'wave-01';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="0340-wave-02-month-line" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET tokens = (tokens - 'cal-othermonth' - 'cal-othermonth-weekend')
             || $J${"cal-month-line": "#8fa8bd"}$J$::jsonb
WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET tokens = (tokens - 'cal-month-line')
             || $J${"cal-othermonth": "#cbe1f6", "cal-othermonth-weekend": "#bed6ed"}$J$::jsonb
WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
